 "rulebook": "No federation rule book: the low-wire crawl of military obstacle courses and obstacle-course racing (wires strung about 18 in, 0.45 m, above the ground; the athlete passes under all of them and may not go round or over). The layout is this benchmark's: wires every 0.5 m over 10 m",
 "deviations": [
  "the wires: each wire is a rigid, fixed bar 8 mm thick between two posts, not a slack (barbed) wire, because the simulator has rigid bodies only; touching one fails the attempt, as a judge's fault for a snagged wire",
  "the ground: level and rigid with a friction coefficient of 1.0, not sand or mud, because the simulator's ground is rigid"
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Get under the low wires in front of you and crawl the whole course until your whole body is beyond the last wire, without touching a wire.",
  "rules": "The obstacle is a lane along +x, 2.0 m wide between two rows of posts, centred on y = 0. Horizontal wires cross it every 0.5 m over 10.0 m: the first is 1.0 m ahead of where your pelvis starts, the last 10.0 m further on. Each wire is 0.008 m thick with its centre 0.45 m above the ground. You succeed when your whole body (every part of you) is beyond the last wire, having passed under all of them. There is no fall rule: any part of you may touch the ground, and you need not stand up at the end. You fail the moment any part of you touches a wire; if your pelvis, while it is between the first and the last wire, is higher than 0.45 m (going over) or outside the lane (going round, beyond a row of posts); if your whole body is beyond the last wire without your pelvis having passed under the wires; or after 120 s. The posts may be touched.",
  "venue": "You stand upright on level ground facing the obstacle (+x), on its centre line, your pelvis 1.0 m before the first wire. You are 1.32 m tall and your pelvis is 0.79 m high when you stand: the wires are lower than your hips. The posts stand at the two ends of every wire, 2.0 m apart; the ground under the wires is the same level, rigid ground. The last wire is painted yellow.",
  "difficulty": "Neither built-in gait works below 0.45 m, and on hands and knees this robot is about 0.46 m high, just too tall: it has to get down from standing and move 10.0 m and its own length flat on the ground with joint commands of its own, never lifting any part into a wire."
 },
